DESIGN DECISIONS
-----------------
1. Embedding model: sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
   - 384 dimensions, cosine distance
   - ~80MB download, CPU-only, no GPU required
   - normalize_embeddings=True ensures cosine similarity via dot product

2. fraud_similarity collection
   - Text representation: "Province X income Y employment Z status W filing V fraud F"
   - Payload: application_id, customer_id, taxable_income, employment_type, province, risk_score, is_fraud
   - Point ID: UUID5(DNS namespace, application_id) — stable, idempotent upserts

3. regulatory_kb collection
   - 50 synthetic chunks from 5 source documents:
       Income_Tax_Act_58_1962 (10 sections)
       Tax_Administration_Act_28_2011 (10 sections)
       SARS_Tax_Tables_2024 (8 brackets + threshold)
       VAT_Act_89_1991 (5 sections)
       SARS_Fraud_Prevention_Policy (8 sections)
       PAYE_Employer_Guide_2024 (7 sections)
   - Point ID: UUID5(DNS namespace, source_doc::section) — idempotent
   - Payload: chunk_id, source_doc, section, text

4. [Risk 3] Preflight guard in seed_qdrant.py
   - bucket_has_files(BUCKET_CLEANED) called before embed_tax_records
   - Exits with clear error if cleaned-tax bucket is empty
   - --skip-preflight flag for testing with synthetic data
   - --kb-only flag skips preflight entirely (KB has no MinIO dependency)

5. Qdrant collections not yet created — will be created on first run of seed_qdrant.py
   Command: python scripts/seed_qdrant.py --kb-only  (safe to run now)
            python scripts/seed_qdrant.py            (run after make submit-sql + wait for cleaned data)

USAGE
------
# Seed regulatory KB now (no MinIO data needed):
python scripts/seed_qdrant.py --kb-only

# Seed fraud records after Flink job_05 has produced cleaned data:
python scripts/seed_qdrant.py

# Or via Makefile:
make seed

QDRANT SEARCH API
-----------------
from agents.qdrant_search import search_similar_fraud, search_regulatory_kb

results = search_similar_fraud({
    "province": "GAUTENG",
    "taxable_income": 750000,
    "employment_type": "SELF_EMPLOYED",
    "employment_status": "ACTIVE",
    "filing_status": "INDIVIDUAL",
}, top_k=5)

results = search_regulatory_kb("What is the penalty for late tax filing?", top_k=3)
context = format_kb_context(results)  # formats into RAG prompt string
